Tips & Tricks

✅ Always check if the array is sorted.

✅ Think about moving one pointer or both pointers based on the condition.

✅ If the current value is too small, move the left pointer.

✅ If the current value is too large, move the right pointer.

✅ Avoid nested loops when two pointers can solve the problem.

✅ Dry run the algorithm before coding.

---

Interview Checklist

- Is the array sorted?
- Can I use left and right pointers?
- Can I reduce O(n²) to O(n)?
- Are duplicate elements present?
- What should happen after moving each pointer?

